### Bloque A — Demo End-to-End de la API Pokémon TCG
### ===================================================
### Requisito: servidor Spring Boot corriendo en localhost:8080
### Base de datos poblada con cartas (POST /api/cards/sync?set=xy1)
###
### Todos los endpoints /api/games/{id}/actions usan body plano (sin payload anidado).
### El frontend envía cardInstanceId (UUID de la copia concreta) o cardId (ID global pokemontcg.io).
### La API traduce internamente al ActionRequest que la fachada espera.

### ===================================================
### A. AUTH
### ===================================================

### Registrar player 1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "demo_p1",
  "email": "demo_p1@test.com",
  "password": "pass123"
}

### Registrar player 2
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "demo_p2",
  "email": "demo_p2@test.com",
  "password": "pass123"
}

### Login player 1 → guardar TOKEN1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "demo_p1",
  "password": "pass123"
}

### Login player 2 → guardar TOKEN2
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "demo_p2",
  "password": "pass123"
}

### ===================================================
### B. CARDS (público, sin token)
### ===================================================

### Listar cartas disponibles
GET http://localhost:8080/api/cards?page=0&size=5

### Buscar cartas por nombre
GET http://localhost:8080/api/cards?name=Pikachu&page=0&size=10

### Carta específica
GET http://localhost:8080/api/cards/xy1-1

### ===================================================
### C. DECKS (requieren token)
### ===================================================
### IMPORTANTE: Reemplazar {{TOKEN1}} y {{TOKEN2}}
### con los tokens obtenidos en los login.
### Ajustar cardIds según las cartas disponibles en BD.

### Player 1 crea mazo
POST http://localhost:8080/api/decks
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{TOKEN1}}

{
  "name": "Mazo Demo 1",
  "cards": [
    {"cardId": "xy1-1", "quantity": 4},
    {"cardId": "base1-1", "quantity": 56}
  ]
}

### Player 2 crea mazo
POST http://localhost:8080/api/decks
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{TOKEN2}}

{
  "name": "Mazo Demo 2",
  "cards": [
    {"cardId": "xy1-1", "quantity": 4},
    {"cardId": "base1-1", "quantity": 56}
  ]
}

### ===================================================
### D. GAME — FLUJO COMPLETO
### ===================================================
### IMPORTANTE: Reemplazar DECK1_ID, DECK2_ID, GAME_ID
### con los valores obtenidos en respuestas anteriores.

### 1. Player 1 crea partida
POST http://localhost:8080/api/games
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{TOKEN1}}

{
  "deckId": {{DECK1_ID}}
}

### 2. Player 2 se une
POST http://localhost:8080/api/games/{{GAME_ID}}/join
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{TOKEN2}}

{
  "deckId": {{DECK2_ID}}
}

### 3. Player 1 consulta estado
### activePokemon = null, bench = [] hasta que se juegue PLAY_BASIC_POKEMON
GET http://localhost:8080/api/games/{{GAME_ID}}/state
Authorization: Bearer {{TOKEN1}}

### 4. Player 2 consulta estado (handSize, prizeCards ocultos)
### activePokemon = null también para player2
GET http://localhost:8080/api/games/{{GAME_ID}}/state
Authorization: Bearer {{TOKEN2}}

### 5. Player 1 juega PLAY_BASIC_POKEMON (primera acción del juego)
### Reemplazar cardInstanceId con uno de los devueltos en el state.
### La API traduce internamente cardInstanceId al ActionRequest que la fachada espera.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/games/{{GAME_ID}}/actions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{TOKEN1}}

{
  "type": "PLAY_BASIC_POKEMON",
  "cardInstanceId": "p1-xy1-1-a1b2c3d4",
  "targetPosition": "ACTIVE"
}

### 6. Player 1 juega END_TURN
POST http://localhost:8080/api/games/{{GAME_ID}}/actions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{TOKEN1}}

{
  "type": "END_TURN"
}

### 7. Player 2 consulta estado (ahora es su turno)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/games/{{GAME_ID}}/state
Authorization: Bearer {{TOKEN2}}

### 8. Player 2 juega USE_ATTACK
POST http://localhost:8080/api/games/{{GAME_ID}}/actions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{TOKEN2}}

{
  "type": "USE_ATTACK",
  "attackIndex": 0
}

### 9. Player 2 juega END_TURN
POST http://localhost:8080/api/games/{{GAME_ID}}/actions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{TOKEN2}}

{
  "type": "END_TURN"
}

### ===================================================
### E. ERRORES
### ===================================================

### Fuera de turno (p2 juega cuando es turno de p1)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/games/{{GAME_ID}}/actions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{TOKEN2}}

{
  "type": "END_TURN"
}

### Acción con error de negocio (fase incorrecta)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/games/{{GAME_ID}}/actions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{TOKEN1}}

{
  "type": "USE_ATTACK",
  "attackIndex": 0
}

### Estado de partida a la que no pertenece
GET http://localhost:8080/api/games/{{GAME_ID}}/state
Authorization: Bearer {{TOKEN1}}_WRONG

### ===================================================
### F. WEBSOCKET (para usar en navegador/consola)
### ===================================================
### Conexión: new SockJS('http://localhost:8080/ws')
### Suscribir: /topic/games/{GAME_ID}/events
### Suscribir: /topic/games/{GAME_ID}/state-changed
### Enviar: /app/game/ping → recibe en /topic/game/pong
